define common-divisor: d is a common divisor of a and b means
       d ∈ ℤ and d divides a and d divides b                           (D1)
       reads d divides both a and b

theorem a-common-divisor-divides-the-first
  note        A phrase whose words write "and" is bracketed beside "and", as
              betweenness is.
  let a ∈ ℤ                                                           (H1)
  let b ∈ ℤ                                                           (H2)
  let d ∈ ℤ                                                           (H3)
  assume (d is a common divisor of a and b) and d > 0                 (H4)
  then d divides a

1.  d is a common divisor of a and b
    restate H4

2.  d ∈ ℤ and d divides a and d divides b
    D1, from 1

3.  d divides a
    restate 2
